# Attach a picked board to the tcp as a collision box, /scene/attach_board (decision-log 5n, S-3 / S-4).
# Call only after the gripper reports vacuum achieved (F12). One board at a time. Metres / radians.
# RULE (S-11): if this board was added as an obstacle (/scene/add_box), remove it first (/scene/remove_box),
# else the attached box overlaps it and every motion fails with START_STATE_IN_COLLISION.
# Board frame = tcp frame turned by yaw about tcp z, centre shifted by (dx, dy) in the tcp frame.
# The box hangs under the cup: from the cup tip (tcp z = 0) to height - contact_margin along tcp +z
# (out of the cup). The margin keeps the box clear of the surface it rests on (lift / place in contact).
float64 length            # along board x (= tcp x when yaw = 0)
float64 width             # along board y
float64 height            # board thickness, along tcp z
float64 yaw               # board rotation about tcp z
float64 dx                # board centre offset from the cup, tcp frame
float64 dy
float64 contact_margin    # 0 -> config default (0.002); must be < height
---
bool success              # false: a board is already attached, bad sizes, MoveIt not reachable
string message
